WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.680
Years after Disney's acquisition of Lucasfilm, the&nbsp;
release of new "Star Wars" movies and TV series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:10.160
has become something of a regular occurrence. In&nbsp;
the early days of Disney "Star Wars," however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:14.480
the franchise's new owners handled the&nbsp;
property at a comparatively slower pace,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:19.200
using their knowledge of the Force to build&nbsp;
huge levels of anticipation before each release.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.280
"That's not how the Force works."

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:25.920
The first two entries in Disney's&nbsp;
"Star Wars" trilogy, then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:28.240
were all the more important&nbsp;
at the time of their release,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:32.080
given that they provided fans with some of their&nbsp;
first insights into the franchise's current&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:36.480
era. Among the key contributions of those&nbsp;
early films was the introduction of Rey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:41.280
portrayed by newcomer Daisy Ridley as Rey.&nbsp;
Adam Driver also stars opposite Ridley as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:46.400
the villainous Kylo Ren, a dark side Jedi as&nbsp;
well as the son of Han Solo and Princess Leia.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:49.760
In an interview with Oh My Disney, Driver&nbsp;
discussed what it was like working with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:54.080
Ridley on Disney's first two Skywalker&nbsp;
saga films, sharing some rare insight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:57.840
into the real-life human being behind one&nbsp;
of the early pillars of modern "Star Wars."

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:02.240
Amidst a larger behind-the-scenes discussion&nbsp;
about their time spent making "Star Wars:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:06.800
The Force Awakens" and "The Last Jedi," Oh My&nbsp;
Disney asked Daisy Ridley and Adam Driver each&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:10.960
what their experience was like working with the&nbsp;
other performer. According to Driver, Ridley was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:15.840
a wholly positive presence on set, both in their&nbsp;
personal interactions and in her acting work.

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:19.200
"It's easy to be in scenes with&nbsp;
her because I could listen to her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:22.720
all day. She has just great instincts."

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:27.200
For what it's worth, Ridley spoke of acting&nbsp;
opposite Driver in similarly glowing terms.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:32.000
"He is so amazing in this film. Seriously.&nbsp;
I can't speak highly enough about him. In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:36.560
the very basic sense of it all, he&nbsp;
is the most amazing scene partner."

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:38.880
By all indications, Ridley appears to be someone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:42.000
alongside whom Driver had a&nbsp;
great time working on-set.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:46.000
As it turns out, Adam Driver's time spent&nbsp;
working with Daisy Ridley ended up blossoming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:50.960
into a full-fledged friendship. Among a number of&nbsp;
other topics — some related to "Star Wars," some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:55.120
not — the two further discussed their relationship&nbsp;
with one another in an interview published by V&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.120 --> 00:02:00.080
Magazine. In fact, it wasn't so much an interview&nbsp;
as a remote conversation between the two.

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:07.840
"I'd rather not do this now. Yeah,&nbsp;
me too. Why did you hate your fath.."

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:14.000
At one point in their conversation, in&nbsp;
response to a question about whether or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:18.000
not she prefers meeting her co-stars prior to&nbsp;
filming, Ridley mentioned that she and Driver&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:22.160
eventually became great friends. The reason&nbsp;
it took so long? Well, it wasn't because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:26.320
they didn't enjoy being with each other&nbsp;
on set. As Ridley said in the interview:

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:30.960
"Adam, we became besties last year, but we had&nbsp;
met some years before. It really takes me a while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:35.520
to relax with people. I don’t think I’m very good&nbsp;
at meeting people: I feel awfully uncomfortable."

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:39.840
Considering the interview's 2017 publication&nbsp;
date, this means that they most likely became&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:44.000
official besties at some point during their time&nbsp;
spent on the set of "The Last Jedi" together.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:48.400
In response, Driver told her, quote, "you always&nbsp;
seemed very open," directly complimenting her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:52.640
personality once again and agreeing that he also&nbsp;
had trouble being comfortable with new people.

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:54.640
Driver also jokingly asked Ridley:

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:57.600
"Is there an aspect of working on&nbsp;
Star Wars—it could be anything from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.600 --> 00:02:59.920
the light saber battles, the travel, the catering,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:03.200
to getting to see me every day and do&nbsp;
my hair—that was your favorite part?"

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:07.200
To which Ridley replied that, quote, "becoming&nbsp;
besties" with Driver had been the highlight of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:10.640
the whole thing. It certainly seems like&nbsp;
the two have fun talking to each other,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:13.040
and it sounds like they had a great time on set.

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:16.880
Finally, at the very end of their conversation,&nbsp;
Driver once again praised Ridley's skill as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:20.560
performer, signing off by telling her,&nbsp;
quote, "I think you're brilliant."

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:24.400
Their discussion in V Magazine showcases how&nbsp;
the two performers speak of one another in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:28.400
glowing terms while keeping the atmosphere&nbsp;
around them lighthearted all the while.

